WEBVTT

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.150
Do you know this man?

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:09.730
Shirahata Kiichiro!

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:14.290
He's a diplomat who once worked 
for the ambassador to Britain.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:17.990
I believe he's currently 
confined to his villa in Izu.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.830
We suspect this Shirahata has learned the 
specifics of high command's "Grand Strategy."

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.920
Wh-What?!

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:29.380
Someone like Shirahata, of all people?!

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:35.030
He was adamantly opposed to 
joining forces with Germany.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.390
Moreover, he's a Western sympathizer,

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.970
and I hear he has numerous 
close friends in Britain.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.630
In particular, he's known
the British consul general,

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:45.270
Ernest Graham, for ages.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.520
It has not been made public yet,

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:52.820
but Graham suddenly made plans to
return to Britain in the very near future.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:54.960
Don't tell me that Shirahata...

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.830
We can't let the "Grand Strategy,"

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:59.340
our army's most valuable secret,

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:00.990
be leaked to Britain!

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.190
Can't we arrest Shirahata and Graham?

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:10.090
We need concrete evidence 
before we can investigate.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.760
And if we can secure 
the location of the delivery,

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.510
we'll have an extra card to 
play in British negotiations.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:21.210
Not to mention an excuse to suppress 
the Western sympathizers in our country.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.320
This situation requires immediate action.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.180
Use them.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.960
<i>As the embers of world war smoldered</i>

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.150
<i>in autumn of 1937,</i>

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.360
<i>the Imperial Army</i>

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:36.360
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.070
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:40.070
<i>established a clandestine 
spy training agency.</i>

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.120
<i>The histories, names, and even ages</i>

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:46.620
<i>of the elite men who pass its 
rigorous application process</i>

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:50.420
<i>are all treated as top-secret information.</i>

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.880
<i>They easily complete training 
exercises that push them</i>

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:56.380
<i>to their physical and mental limits.</i>

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:59.760
<i>Under the command of founder 
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki,</i>

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.510
<i>they operate worldwide, within the shadows.</i>

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:07.050
<i>And so a brand-new intelligence 
agency was created.</i>

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.790
<i>Its name is "D-Agency."</i>

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:47.370
Yokohama

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:57.540
<b>British Consul's Estate</b>

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:00.230
Check.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:09.720
Episode 8 - Double Joker (Part 1)

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.720
I wasn't prepared for that...

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:15.650
Now I've won 15 and lost 17, with six stalemates.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:19.900
I know you're busy, Consul, so let's call it a day.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:23.650
This program is a work of fiction. 
The characters, organizations, locations, laws, names, 
etc. being portrayed are unrelated to actual events.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.450
Hold on, now.

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.720
We can play one more game.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:24.660
Dear...

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:27.680
Er...

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.580
May I interrupt?

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.610
What's wrong?

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.720
That man at the back gate 
was there yesterday, too.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:40.500
Who?

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.080
He told the maid he's with the waterworks...

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:49.720
But something about him unnerves me.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.520
What do you think?

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.890
He's probably a military policeman.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:57.560
Why do you say that?

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.570
His face is very tan.

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:05.050
But from his forehead up, 
his skin's oddly pale.

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:09.280
Therefore, his real job must not only 
have him walking around outside all day,

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.900
but also require him to 
wear a hat while on duty.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:13.780
If he's not wearing his hat now,

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:17.620
it's because it would be a dead 
giveaway of his real job.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.900
The only occupation I can think of

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:22.760
that requires a specific hat, 
and that one would keep secret,

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.010
is military policeman.

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:28.520
Or something like it, yes.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:30.750
Surprising, right?

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:33.380
For a kid his age,

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:36.440
and a Japanese at that, he's quite sharp.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.150
Mr. Gamou,

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:42.010
Japan is heading further and 
further down the wrong path.

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:44.400
Its actions in China,

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.750
and now, sending spies to our home...

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:48.240
It's shameful.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.850
No! Jane, stop it.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:55.450
Mr. Gamou is employed by Taylor 
Terashima and is a friend of mine.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:58.580
He's not affiliated with Japan's 
government or military.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.060
Yes... You're right.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.170
I apologize, Mr. Gamou.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:06.920
It's all right, no offense taken.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:10.220
Go out, get some fresh air, and try to relax.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:10.850
Yes.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:13.890
And take the parasol I bought you.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:17.010
I don't want your face ending up like that MP's.

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:19.440
Sorry about that.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.150
She's not used to the climate here,

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.700
so she's been having trouble sleeping at night.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:26.970
Now, shall we continue the competition?

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.370
I'm afraid I'll have to decline.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.190
I have some business

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.540
with one other customer today.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:39.000
In that case, I suppose we'll have to wait.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.330
We'll pick up next time.

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.110
Take care.

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:50.680
Thank you.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:10.240
<i>Imbecile.</i>

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:13.030
<i>Spying is a job for a gentleman.</i>

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:16.700
<i>A lowlife like him could 
never make it as a spy.</i>

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.580
<b>Mooncakes</b>

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.580
<b>Mid-Autumn Festival</b>

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.010
Chou-san.

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.260
What's going on?

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:24.190
I could see you were tailing me.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.690
Yes, on Graham-san's orders.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:30.580
Why?

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.240
I don't know why, specifically,

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:37.240
but he's been extremely 
high-strung this past week.

00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:41.450
It's not just you. He's had nearly all 
his visitors tailed after they leave.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:47.470
I was scared that he might've found 
out you introduced me to this place.

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:50.840
No, I believe it's work-related.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:54.080
He was excited about getting 
promoted if things went well...

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:56.840
Has anything else changed?

00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:09.730
Graham-san is going to leave Japan soon.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:12.870
He received some confidential 
orders from back home.

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:14.620
For what reason?

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:20.240
He hasn't told the servants any of the details.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.530
I see.

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:26.280
Well, do enjoy yourself this evening...

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:28.790
Or so I'd like to say...

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:33.200
But you still haven't paid back the 
money I loaned you the other day.

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:37.040
Please, can you wait just one more week?

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:41.170
I've lent you a total of 15,000 yen.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:44.680
A whole five years' worth of your salary.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:48.400
You're not going to get that in a week.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.000
There's nothing left to say.

00:09:58.310 --> 00:09:59.740
W-Wait, please.

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:02.720
Three days! I swear I'll get the money!

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:05.130
A-At this rate, I'll...

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:08.510
I-I'm begging you. I'll do anything!

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:26.830
Take care.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.790
<i>Chess is a simple game, 
but it's that very simplicity</i>

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.620
<i>that makes the players' 
personalities come out.</i>

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:46.500
<i>What chess taught me about 
Graham's personality is...</i>

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:48.460
<i>He's simple.</i>

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:52.720
<i>And yet, he's eager to carry out his plans.</i>

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:00.060
<i>He's twice as cautious as the average person.</i>

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:04.930
<i>A show-off. Ambitious.</i>

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:09.890
<i>The information to be gained from 
the "Grand Strategy" could earn him</i>

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:12.140
<i>a prominent position in Britain.</i>

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:14.720
<i>He must want it so badly he can taste it.</i>

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:17.210
<i>My gut feeling is that he's "black."</i>

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:23.620
<i>That's clear from the way he's had 
Chou follow his guests all week.</i>

00:11:30.050 --> 00:11:33.630
<i>But I haven't seen a single 
trace of any attempts</i>

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.880
<i>by Graham to contact anyone.</i>

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:40.090
<i>The circumstances suggest he's "white."</i>

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:44.500
You saw through me, huh?

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:49.800
Such novice diversionary tactics won't fool me.

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:52.550
You're a step above me when it comes

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:54.830
to both perception and deception.

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:57.780
Trying to get me to lower my guard?

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:08.050
<i>I guess I'll have to confirm things myself.</i>

00:12:13.910 --> 00:12:17.800
Get the guard on duty to take this drug.

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:19.360
It's tasteless and odorless.

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:22.390
Mixed into a drink, it's undetectable.

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:26.340
There's nothing to worry about.

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:28.280
It's just a knockout drug,

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.180
and I'll only take the money.

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:33.340
If nobody causes trouble, 
nobody will get hurt.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:37.820
I hate to sound repetitive, but the 
money's inside the safe, correct?

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:38.880
Yes.

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:43.250
We split it 50-50. That's 20,000 apiece.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:50.410
Besides, that money came from the 
English selling opium all over China.

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:52.770
There's no reason to feel guilty about it.

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:55.360
As you instructed,

00:12:55.360 --> 00:12:58.200
I had a duplicate safe key made.

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:01.120
I just need to leave the 
front door unlocked, right?

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:49.320
<i>Nothing.</i>

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:52.600
<i>I've gone through everything in the safe,</i>

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:57.480
<i>but there's nothing about getting the 
"Grand Strategy" from Shirahata.</i>

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:00.490
<i>The only thing left is this journal...</i>

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:03.910
<i>I guess Graham is "white" after all?</i>

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:09.490
I received the umbrella I ordered.
I'll give it to Jane tomorrow.

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:09.290
<i>This was a present for his wife?</i>

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:13.200
Go out, get some fresh air, and try to relax.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:13.770
Yes.

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:16.710
And take the parasol I bought you.

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:20.240
I don't want your face ending up like that MP's.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:30.690
Is someone there?

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:39.970
Satisfied now? Let's go to bed.

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:54.700
Is something wrong?

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:57.090
No, it was nothing.

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:19.490
After investigating,

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:22.210
I can confirm Graham is "black."

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.260
I found an incriminating message

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:28.880
in the hollowed-out handle of 
the umbrella he gave to his wife.

00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:32.210
He used his wife as a messenger,

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:34.800
but the woman herself was unaware.

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:41.040
I marked it with the special ink 
you loaned me, and followed her.

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:45.290
It was on the fingers of the maitre'd 
at a nearby restaurant,

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.880
the cloakroom coat checker
at a building she entered,

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:53.540
and the waiter at a coffee shop.

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:56.470
And, of course,

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:01.000
on Ernest Graham's fingertips.

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:05.580
Shirahata's plan

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:09.420
is to hand over the information 
at his Izu villa in one week,

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:13.030
and for Graham to immediately 
return to England afterwards.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:22.000
<b>Mooncakes</b>

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:22.000
<b>Mid-Autumn Festival</b>

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:25.460
<b>Mooncakes</b>

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:27.050
What the hell?

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:29.750
No money was stolen from the safe!

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:33.380
I know. Change of plans.

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:35.270
What about my money?!

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:36.730
I did everything you asked—

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:38.450
Just relax.

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:43.130
That money...

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:45.810
What did you...

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:01.080
Here's 20,000.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:04.240
And I'll call off the debt you owe me, too.

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:35.200
I killed my accomplice, Chou,

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.990
by making it appear as 
if he tried to rob me.

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:42.210
There's absolutely no evidence 
linking me to his death.

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:45.910
That concludes my report.

00:17:47.490 --> 00:17:49.160
Kill without hesitation.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:50.950
Die with honor.

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:54.960
You're now officially a part of "Wind Agency."

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:04.560
<b>Six Months Earlier</b>

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:14.140
A pleasure to see you again,
Akutsu, Your Excellency.

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:16.200
Relax.

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:19.170
Officially, this visit isn't happening.

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:22.940
You and I never met today.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:24.370
Sir.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:30.630
I received your report the other day.

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:34.450
Summarize the situation for me, 
Lieutenant Colonel Kazato Akimasa.

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:35.560
Sir.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:41.260
Information is becoming more and 
more critical in modern warfare.

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:43.950
It's plain as the nose on your face that,

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:46.360
today, there are spies 
from all over the world

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:48.410
operating in the imperial capital.

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:50.590
To defend our secrets

00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:53.210
from the spies of the world powers,

00:18:54.350 --> 00:18:56.560
I believe it's imperative that

00:18:56.560 --> 00:19:00.160
we establish intelligence schools and 
espionage agencies as soon as possible.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:07.440
Since the founding of 
the empire in the Meiji era,

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:11.380
we've fought our battles without 
such cowardly tactics as using spies.

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:13.540
The Imperial Army prides itself

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:15.840
on fighting fair and square.

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:17.890
To trifle with crafty strategies

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:21.250
is an insult to the army's honor!

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:23.670
Now...

00:19:24.210 --> 00:19:26.640
That isn't how I actually feel.

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:29.020
It's the majority opinion within the army.

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:32.830
The truth is, there's already

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:35.730
a secret spy agency within the army.

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:40.300
Let me guess, you've never 
heard of such an agency?

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:43.900
It was founded about a year ago.

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:45.950
They call it "D-Agency."

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:49.710
The founder, also a lieutenant 
colonel, started it himself.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:53.710
However, D-Agency is 
a horse of a different color

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.480
compared to what you proposed.

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:58.090
"Don't die. Don't kill."

00:19:58.910 --> 00:20:01.860
Despite being part of the Imperial Army,

00:20:02.330 --> 00:20:05.800
they're using local civilians 
to carry out their plans.

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:07.990
Impossible.

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:11.000
Why would a spy agency,

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:14.290
of all things, be using citizens?

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:16.870
"We can't use War College grads."

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:19.330
What did you say?

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:22.170
The words of D-Agency's founder, Yuuki.

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:25.030
"I can't use military men.

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:27.830
I won't even accidentally allow anyone from

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.840
the Army War College through my doors."

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:30.990
His words.

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:34.180
Yuuki...

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:43.130
Kill without hesitation. Die with honor.

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:48.940
Throughout the course of your studies,

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:50.810
that's the kind of logical methodology

00:20:51.070 --> 00:20:52.640
you'll need to rely on

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:55.410
as members of the Imperial 
Army's espionage agency.

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:06.240
I'm told you connected
Shirahata to Graham.

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:09.140
Can you secure the location 
of the exchange?

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:13.710
Yes. I've already planted an 
operative inside Shirahata's villa.

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:17.670
So preparations are complete, then.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:20.880
Once you successfully 
complete this operation,

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:22.390
your "Wind Agency" will be

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:26.390
officially recognized as the 
Imperial Army's espionage agency.

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:29.100
I expect great things.

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:36.310
D-Agency has also been informed 
of the Shirahata situation.

00:21:37.450 --> 00:21:39.970
I have no intention of 
